WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.800
The real case for universal basic income
in my view is not financial, it is moral.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.190
To live a satisfying life

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:19.350
a person must spend that life doing
important things such as raising a

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:25.650
family, holding a job that is satisfying
and fulfilling, being a good member of

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:30.660
one's community. For those roles to be
satisfying, people have to have

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.850
responsibility for what those
institutions do. Have responsibility for

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:39.719
the decisions they make. One of the
things that the lucky people in society

00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:45.510
already have is a life in which they
know they can take responsibility for

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:46.710
their own actions;

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:52.559
they can live the lives they see fit. What
a universal basic income will do is make

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:55.800
that same possibility for a satisfying
life

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:01.289
open to everyone, and that would be a
fulfillment of the American dream that

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:05.820
goes far beyond the usual notions of a
nice house in the suburbs.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:12.250
 

